# Mosquitto ACL for the phone's local broker: example, not installed by any script here.
# Installing it is the owner's step (docs/event-bus.md, "Broker ACL"). Event bus: mcp-prompts#140.
#
# Mosquitto ACLs only grant: a topic not granted to a client is refused (publish dropped,
# subscription refused). There is no "deny" line. So every prefix the phone's local clients use
# must be listed below, or that client stops working.

# --- Anonymous clients (lines before the first `user`; needs allow_anonymous true) ----------
# Keeps today's credential-less clients working: MIA, zigbee2mqtt, and the android-assistant
# MCP server until it has credentials (mqtt_publish allows only mia/* and zigbee2mqtt/*).
# Add a line for every other prefix your local clients use (watch `mosquitto_sub -v -t '#'`
# for a while before enabling the ACL). Nothing on phone/events/# for anonymous clients: they
# can neither fake an event nor read one.
topic readwrite mia/#
topic readwrite zigbee2mqtt/#

# --- Tasker publisher (phone/tasker/event-publish.sh) ---------------------------------------
# Publish only, and only phone events.
user phone-tasker
topic write phone/events/#

# --- Agents (android-assistant MCP server: wait_event, mqtt_publish) ------------------------
# Read the phone events, never publish them. Write what mqtt_publish already allows (its own
# allowlist and confirmations still apply on top).
user phone-agent
topic read phone/events/#
topic write mia/#
topic write zigbee2mqtt/#
